    "content": "Health is a comprehensive state of physical, mental, and social well-being, not just the absence of disease, encompassing areas like nutrition, exercise, and sleep. Key issues include obesity and chronic illness, while trends focus on preventative care and whole-health approaches. Major organizations include the WHO and local health departments. Main Types of Health Physical: Functioning of the body, influenced by diet, activity, and sleep. Mental/Emotional: Cultivating a healthy mind and managing stress. Social: Building supportive networks. Spiritual: Finding purpose and balance. Major Health Issues (US & Global) Obesity: Over 40% of the US population is obese. Chronic Disease: Issues like diabetes, cardiovascular disease, and cancer. Mental Health: Rising focus on anxiety, depression, and overall well-being. Injuries: Bone fractures and burns are common worldwide. Environmental Factors: Pollution and exposure to toxins. Current Trends in Health Preventative Care: Early screenings (mammograms, colonoscopies) and regular checkups. Lifestyle Medicine: Focus on nutrition (plant-based diets), exercise, and avoiding tobacco. Whole Health: A shift towards holistic care that includes emotional and social factors, not just physical symptoms. Technology Integration: Using technology to improve healthcare delivery. Major Health Organizations World Health Organization (WHO): Sets global health standards. National Institutes of Health (NIH): Conducts medical research. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC): Protects public health in the US. Local/State Health Departments: Manage community health. Key Habits for Good Health Eating a diet rich in fruits, vegetables, and lean proteins. Engaging in regular physical activity. Getting 7-9 hours of quality sleep. Managing stress and maintaining social connections. Regular medical screenings and checkups.",
